<article class="env-definition" id="03RW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03RW">Definition <span data-tag="03RW">59.71.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
A sheaf of sets on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$ is <em>constructible</em> if for every affine open $U \subset X$ there exists a finite decomposition of $U$ into constructible locally closed subschemes $U = \coprod _ i U_ i$ such that $\mathcal{F}|_{U_ i}$ is finite locally constant for all $i$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A sheaf of abelian groups on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$ is <em>constructible</em> if for every affine open $U \subset X$ there exists a finite decomposition of $U$ into constructible locally closed subschemes $U = \coprod _ i U_ i$ such that $\mathcal{F}|_{U_ i}$ is finite locally constant for all $i$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Let $\Lambda $ be a Noetherian ring. A sheaf of $\Lambda $-modules on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$ is <em>constructible</em> if for every affine open $U \subset X$ there exists a finite decomposition of $U$ into constructible locally closed subschemes $U = \coprod _ i U_ i$ such that $\mathcal{F}|_{U_ i}$ is of finite type and locally constant for all $i$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>